      "summary": "Former Spanish Prime Minister José María Aznar traveled to Ceuta on Thursday while the city was facing a crisis caused by a large influx of migrants. His visit came after he publicly criticized the national government’s handling of the situation, accusing it of incapacity and of adopting a submissive policy toward Morocco. The trip occurred during heightened tensions and media attention focused on the mass entry of migrants into the Spanish enclave.",
      "takeaway": "Aznar’s Ceuta visits escalate political scrutiny of the government’s migration and Morocco policies, intensifying domestic pressure and debate.",
      "why_it_matters": "The visits by former Prime Minister José María Aznar to Ceuta, coupled with his criticisms of the current government’s handling of migrant arrivals and relations with Morocco, publicly amplify political pressure on Spain’s government and contribute to domestic debate over migration policy and bilateral diplomacy—affecting political actors, public discourse, and Spain’s stance toward Morocco."
